Z||000000||Dad of 5||08-23-99||04:28 PM||||I have stripped the bolts that hold the TPS to the injector housing on an 84 2.5.  I have checked several sources in my area for the bolts and they are not available.  Pontiac stopped selling them several years ago.  Is there anyone out there who can tell me where I can obtaine a set of these bolts or what the correct size is so I can replace the with something else?
Z||000001||theogre||08-23-99||04:34 PM||||IF Only the bolts are damaged then they can be replaced with any common metric thread screw of the same length and thread pitch. Otherwise if you want exact replacements you will need to go to a scrap yard.
Z||000002||Dale||08-24-99||02:37 AM||||I just got a new tps and it actualy came with some new bolts.  I dont need them so if you cant find any I will mail them to you.  The only drawback is they are a hex head only.  My E-mail is reefscape@mciworld.com  Let me know if you need them.
Z||000003||Dale||08-25-99||01:45 AM||||Your bolts are on thier way.<p>Aloha
